id: pm-8kzfc4
title: Explain binding token budgets beside read-output alias migration hints
description: "GitHub issue #1222 reports that output_budget_reached responses suggest migrating --limit to --output-limit without naming the binding token ceiling. Existing cursor continuation and monotonic recovery primitives are delivered by pm-8nev0o and pm-xam9bt; this residual UX defect concerns the adjacent migration_hints and list help. Add a cause-specific bounded recovery hint shared by SDK CLI and MCP, retain alias guidance, and prove that the prescribed retry changes the binding budget."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-08T15:32:57.518Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T23:33:29.391Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-08T23:33:28.846Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-08T23:33:28.846Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Budget truncation emits a cause-specific retry beside legacy alias guidance; increasing the named budget returns more rows; exhausted session budgets name the session option; canonical alias migration remains equivalent independently of token limits.
parent: pm-5t33or
severity: low
repro_steps: Request list output above the default token ceiling with --limit; inspect migration_hints and retry using only the recommended --output-limit alias.
resolution: "Budget recovery identifies command and session ceilings, preserves alias guidance, and resumes withheld rows through the documented recovery cursor and transport bindings. The public type and guide explicitly define restore_with=recovery as a reference."
expected_result: Agents can resolve the declared recovery object and continue without repeated or skipped rows while preserving token ceilings.
actual_result: "The existing session consumer regression executes the returned reference and SDK binding. All 13 focused recovery and real transport tests, linked verification, build, four typechecks, docs, static/docstrings, ESLint and snapshots pass. Runtime JavaScript is unchanged. Previous exact-head preflight passed 8623 tests at 100/100/100/100; final-head hosted gates and full review govern merge."
component: sdk/read-output
regression: false
customer_impact: Agents can waste repeated calls changing row limits while the token budget remains binding.
